    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are positioned for a high-ceiling outing today, headlined by **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56) and **Gunnar Henderson** (75.31). **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** represents our most aggressive play against Adrian Houser; the matchup against a high-xERA arm combined with the favorable wind conditions creates an elite environment for him to drive production. Similarly, **Gunnar Henderson** remains a must-start despite facing a formidable arm in Logan Gilbert. While the opposing SP skill drags his base projection down, the positive park factors and the wind blowing out mitigate that risk, ensuring **Gunnar Henderson** retains his status as our offensive engine. **Curtis Mead** (63.58) also benefits significantly from the Houser matchup, making our middle infield exposure the cornerstone of today\u2019s strategy.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Nolan Schanuel** (54.71), who narrowly missed the cut over **Jackson Merrill** (53.33). While **Nolan Schanuel** offers a stable floor, we opted to ride the upside of **Jackson Merrill** against Chase Burns, favoring the dynamic platoon advantage. Managing our daily efficiency caps remains a priority, which forced us to bench **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (52.86) as well; facing a high-tier arm like Zack Wheeler creates too much risk for a sub-60 score when we have more favorable matchups elsewhere. We are tracking **Brayan Rocchio** closely, but with a 43% rain risk hovering over his contest, he is an easy bench candidate for today.\n\nInvestors should note the volatility surrounding our lineup-pending slots, specifically **Nasim Nunez** (59.37), **Curtis Mead**, and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** While we are counting on their projected spots, any shift down the order will adjust their efficiency scores downward. Furthermore, **Kyle Tucker** (47.91) and **Andy Pages** (44.65) face the toughest test of the day against Paul Skenes. Their scores are suppressed by Skenes\u2019 elite stuff and a wind-in forecast, but their elite sprint speed and positional value keep them in the mix to maintain our competitive edge in the stolen base category despite the tough matchup.",
